  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Coronado Springs is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want Moderate pricing with more dining than a typical Moderate.</strong> In 2026 a Village Standard Location room ran about $294 to $470 a night at full price, tax included, which is the lowest starting Moderate rate in this batch.</li>
      <li><strong>People who want a tower room, a club lounge, or a water view</strong> without moving up to a Deluxe resort. Gran Destino Tower is a different product from the village rooms.</li>
      <li><strong>Convention-goers</strong> who want to stay on site, with the caveat below.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You want the Skyliner, a monorail or a boat.</strong> Buses are the only free Disney transportation from here.</li>
      <li><strong>Construction around El Centro would bother you.</strong> Official pages say the convention center is under planned refurbishment from August 10, 2026, through late September 2027, with related work in the El Centro Corridor. Guests may see or hear construction.</li>
      <li><strong>You want a compact resort.</strong> The village sections are spread around the lake. Preferred village rooms are closer to El Centro.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
