  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Start with a Village Standard Location room if the Tower is not the point.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran about $294 to $470 a night at full price including tax, depending on dates. Preferred village rooms ran about $426 to $573.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay more for the Tower only if you will use it.</strong> In 2026 a Tower Resort View room ran about $376 to $670. Water View and Club Access rooms were higher. Compare that with a Deluxe resort before you book.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra adults cost more.</strong> Moderate rates assume two adults. Each extra adult adds $25 a night plus tax, and kids under 18 are free.</li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="fg-callout">
      <h3>Rates change</h3>
      <p style="margin:0">The rate range above is MouseSavers' October 2026 snapshot of Disney's full prices, not a deal. Always check the live price on Disney's site before you book.</p>
